{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 40,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David. I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined to me, and heard my cry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He brought me up also out of a horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " established my goings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he hath put a new song in my mouth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " praise to our God: many shall see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that man that maketh the LORD his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many, O LORD, my God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy wonderful works ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast done, and thy thoughts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " toward us, they cannot be reckoned up in order to thee: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I would declare and speak ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they are more than can be numbered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; my ears hast thou opened: burnt-offering and sin-offering hast thou not required.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said I, Lo, I come: in the volume of the book ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " written of me,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I delight to do thy will, O my God: yea, thy law ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " within my heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: lo, I have not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy loving-kindness and thy truth from the great congregation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O LORD: let thy loving-kindness and thy truth continually preserve me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For innumerable evils have encompassed me: my iniquities have taken hold upon me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of my head: therefore my heart faileth me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me: O LORD, make haste to help me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it; let them be driven backward and put to shame that wish me evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame that say to me, Aha, aha.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The LORD be magnified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.40.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.40.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " poor and needy; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thinketh upon me: thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my help and my deliverer; make no delay, O my God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
